{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy","id":1016043,"title":"Telepathy and the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T03:09:53-08:00","id":1016043,"title":"Telepathy and the Technocracy","content":"Just a thought, do you it's possible for a Technocrat to practice telepathy in the technocratic paradigm? What about other &quot;mind powers&quot; like pyrokinesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12015-elstren","name":"Elstren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T03:53:52-08:00","id":1016049,"title":"","content":"Oh, definitely<br /> The Technocracy employs 'psychics' and other assets that might be..unorthodox and 'experimental' in most of their scientific regards.<br /> Probably more among their Extraordinary Citizens (Psychic numina et al) than their Enlightened Operatives, but they still probably have personnel among both that fall under that category.<br /> <br /> Depending on how the feat is performed, with or without technological aid.<br /> And those assets are probably constantly under close scrutiny and observation for derivation from Technocratic principles and loyalty...but they *are* valuable to the Technocracy in 'Special missions' where a Psychics insight or abilities are needed.<br /> <br /> And, considering that the Traditions usually do not expect the Technocracy to make a resource like that pop up in the field, might be more feared than what they've come to expect.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a reference, I'd like to suggest an old Anime - Witch Hunter Robin - which (aside of thankfully being low on Animeish tropes) is an <i>excellent</i> inspiration along those lines, and could be interpreted as a Technocratic experiment where the employed Psychics are not even quite aware of the full extent of the Technocracy, or the nature of Mages..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-12-2016, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T03:59:11-08:00","id":1016050,"title":"","content":"Technocracy has psionics; they aren't in the spotlight though. The 2nd Progenitor Convention Book has a psionic in the introduction short story - it is mentioned that he needs to synthesize replacement spinal fluid for himself as a result of using his powers.<br /> Psionics could be the result of a permanent biological modification, a special kind of drug, or an implant put into the brain. You could also have implants or drugs shared by Technocrats to give them telepathy within a group. I'd imagine that it's Unmutual to hold the idea that unaided humans can access mind powers like telepathy or pyrokinesis with just concentration and training.<br /> <br /> Of course, the most Technocratic thing a Technocrat can do to read someone's mind, is to simply prod the target in the right way, and then apply knowledge, intuition and analysis skills! They are just <i>that</i> good. (Though I imagine this only works if they analyzed someone beforehand, or have lot of time and resources to interact with them.)<br /> For telepathy in regards to allies, cutting edge coordination and learned, minute cues can make it so that they know each others' thoughts without speaking. You could also have Technocrats capable of simulating conversations with other people in their heads. (or out loud)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-12-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T06:06:17-08:00","id":1016080,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Union prefers technological tools for psionic powers, where it can. It makes them more controllable, and preserves the illusion that what the Union does isn't magic. That said, I can also see them telling their underlings that it's possible for humans to develop psionics through training, if push comes to shove. That way they can handwave away what the traditionalists do.<br /> <br /> Best case scenario, they prefer psychic powers as a result of artifice. Brain implants, nanomachines (son), gene engineering, xeno-grafts, specialized headware (I can see a metal interface band hidden in the lining of a hat), and perhaps even specialized spying equipment installed in a van. Many of these things can be taken away, one way or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1016050#post1016050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the most Technocratic thing a Technocrat can do to read someone's mind, is to simply prod the target in the right way, and then apply knowledge, intuition and analysis skills! They are just <i>that</i> good. (Though I imagine this only works if they analyzed someone beforehand, or have lot of time and resources to interact with them.)<br /> For telepathy in regards to allies, cutting edge coordination and learned, minute cues can make it so that they know each others' thoughts without speaking. You could also have Technocrats capable of simulating conversations with other people in their heads. (or out loud)</div> </div> </div> </div>Union personnel have been reading people's psychology and body language to a scary degree since the days of the Order of Reason. Entire languages of secret hand signs and other signals were developed by the Craftmasons and Ksirafai to facilitate covert communication. So it's certain that the Technocracy has refined and perfected such techniques by the modern day.<br /> <br /> Sure, it's not Telepathy <i>per se</i>, but to a Technocrat the results are the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:45:01-08:00","id":1016118,"title":"","content":"It's rather strange, but psychic powers are more associated with the Technocracy than with the Traditions. They really shouldn't be, given than a lot of what we associate with psychic power grew out of Victorian and New Age spiritualism, both of which the Technocracy largely rejects. However, the untapped potential of the human mind is a staple of utopian thinking and as such appeals to the Technocracy. That's the key element element. The Traditions widely use abilities we would call psychic, but they come bundled with cultural, mystical, or mythical elements that take them away from what we usually think of when we hear 'psychic powers'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:36:33-08:00","id":1016252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1016080#post1016080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Union personnel have been reading people's psychology and body language to a scary degree since the days of the Order of Reason. Entire languages of secret hand signs and other signals were developed by the Craftmasons and Ksirafai to facilitate covert communication. So it's certain that the Technocracy has refined and perfected such techniques by the modern day.<br /> <br /> Sure, it's not Telepathy <i>per se</i>, but to a Technocrat the results are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcannon it can actually become telepathy. As members of an Amalgam get better in reading each other, they tend to drift into using simulacrums - instead of reasoning &quot;What is my partner thinking?&quot;, they turn on an approximation of their partner in their head and listen to it; letting their subconscious do the work. This even works for Technocrats who haven't talked to their partners for years. (Keeping tabs on them or reading their publications enhances the effect.) The Ivory Tower strives to explain the eerily accuracy and synchronization of those simulacrum techniques through psychology and sociology. However, unofficially it is known that agents conversing with a 'simulacrum' have received information that they could have not possible deduced from a mere intellectual simulation - like precise hints about a captured partner's location. It could be called &quot;Technocratic Drill&quot; or &quot;Amalgam Drill&quot;.<br /> And &quot;Technepandi Drill&quot; for the Technepandi. Technepandi, due to being initiated into mysticism, have tested and investigated how exactly it works. They prefer to use it in it's Technocratic almost-telepathy version...but when needed they can reliably direct/steer it with telepathic impulses or other mystic spells.<br /> <br /> You can take it a step further, and say that when a Technocrat needs advice of a close friend, they construct a little shrine of photographs etc., while going through their past e-mails or chat conversations; this enables them to create a very independent and accurate simulacrum to get advice from.<br /> <br /> This has precedence in the Order of Reason; Mind 3 effect Cry of Distress is described thus:<br /> &quot; (...) And as conspiratorial legends tell us, if a brother is in mortal danger, he may give the Cry of Distress, a secret gesture altering Daedaleans nearby that he needs immediate aid.<br /> Brethren and initiates faithfully memorize these covert signals, but in truth, they vary widely from one lodge to another. Oddly enough, scholarly crusaders seem to have an intuitive grasp of nearly all of these signals, even if they're given by someone they've never met from a lodge from far away. Conspiracies are cloaked in mystery, so no one questions the details of such coincidences ...though the masters of the Inner Mysteries sagely nod when those stories are retold in private.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-12-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:52:05-08:00","id":1017229,"title":"","content":"Another way to do Technocratic telepathy: Progenitor pheromones. A Technocrat would have modified organs that secrete chemicals etc. which induce different states of mind. Once they tag you - perhaps with some viruses, bacteria, or spores - they can also use a combination of smell and taste to read your emotions and thoughts from a distance; and adjust as needed. More concrete images can be put into the mind through a combination of a strong pheromone pulse and code-words; or seeding the wanted impression beforehand through sending appropriately-themed spam to the target's e-mail, or with SMSes etc.<br /> <br /> NWO could use a gas or a liquid that makes you extremely suggestive to certain stimuli - it doesn't have to be outright commands...but more like tiny stuff that a trained NWO would work into the interaction to influence your mind. Another kind of substance could make someone more likely to show what they have on their mind.<br /> Yet another possibility is a wave or radiation generator that sends the desired impression; a different type could give a read-out of someone's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-15-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T07:08:05-08:00","id":1017633,"title":"","content":"I think there's the usual conflation and confusion of the effect, as per the description of the Sphere, and the manner of implementation involved., e.g. the Focus<br /> <br /> Telepathy in the sense of psychic mind-reading isn't different from &quot;telepathy&quot; using advanced knowledge of proximics, kinesics and psychology or through or through Muad'Dib's collection of mental &quot;talking heads&quot; or through some kind of at-a-distance electro-neural mapping and something like phreaking someone else's brain (put a chip in their head, or even get them to wear it near their head.. or maybe even just install them in wi-fi as a hidden feature... &quot;What does that circuit do?&quot; &quot;I don't know, but everything on the market has one...&quot;), or through some application of a cocktail of psychoactive chemicals... (in some ways, any truth-drug could be seen as &quot;telepathy&quot; in that it reveals a subject's thoughts, it just does so by getting them to verbalize them). <br /> <br /> Sure, there are limitations on what can be achieved by the different methods used, but that's the way Focus and Spheres always interact. Some things are more difficult, or even impossible to do based on the Focus, but the effect itself is accomplished by any of these means, the others described above and ton of others.<br /> <br /> As for the whole modern psionic telepathy... Well, it's in the books and it's considered a line of research that was previously pursued back in the MK-ULTRA, Cold War era, espionage times, even going so far as beginning to introduce it to the Masses. But it's also stated that it was deep-sixed to a large degree. Taken off the Time Table, etc. It seems like it's a smaller version of what happened to the Etherites, without the consequences... Which means there are definitely some Technocrats out there who were involved in the research (and they might be pissed off that their research was just defunded and de-authorized and all their work left hanging, unless that got conditioned away). The research is also still out there in some NWO Black Archive. There is also a reason why it was taken off the Time Table. if you are a Technephandi fan, maybe the Nephandi masters realized it might increase the chance of their exposure? Otherwise... something happened. Someone make an argument and it was accepted. <br /> <br /> Seems like the fluff side of this issue, more than the mechanical, could lead to a lot of interesting questions that might keep an amalgam/cabal busy. (How about an Etherite looking to acquire all the research notes?) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T07:15:34-08:00","id":1017637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1016252#post1016252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my headcannon it can actually become telepathy. As members of an Amalgam get better in reading each other, they tend to drift into using simulacrums - instead of reasoning &quot;What is my partner thinking?&quot;, they turn on an approximation of their partner in their head and listen to it; letting their subconscious do the work. This even works for Technocrats who haven't talked to their partners for years. (Keeping tabs on them or reading their publications enhances the effect.) The Ivory Tower strives to explain the eerily accuracy and synchronization of those simulacrum techniques through psychology and sociology. However, unofficially it is known that agents conversing with a 'simulacrum' have received information that they could have not possible deduced from a mere intellectual simulation - like precise hints about a captured partner's location. It could be called &quot;Technocratic Drill&quot; or &quot;Amalgam Drill&quot;.<br /> And &quot;Technepandi Drill&quot; for the Technepandi. Technepandi, due to being initiated into mysticism, have tested and investigated how exactly it works. They prefer to use it in it's Technocratic almost-telepathy version...but when needed they can reliably direct/steer it with telepathic impulses or other mystic spells.<br /> <br /> You can take it a step further, and say that when a Technocrat needs advice of a close friend, they construct a little shrine of photographs etc., while going through their past e-mails or chat conversations; this enables them to create a very independent and accurate simulacrum to get advice from.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had something like this happen awhile ago in a chronicle long since put to bed....<br /> <br /> One character was the NWO agent in charge of overseeing dealing with the supernatural occurrences in the city. He was massively understaffed and, effectively, his job was an &quot;unfunded mandate&quot;, but one which he was held responsible for by his dick of a superior. So, at the start of the game, he acquired the remainder of the group and facilitated setting up the group as a his agent provacateurs. <br /> <br /> But, the group was of massively different ways of looking at magic. (Paradigms in those days. More like Practices and Foci now.) To the point that it was hard to discuss how they would apply their abilities to solve issues. And their &quot;magic&quot; gobbledygook was just annoying to the NWO. So he created an effect for their planning meetings (which had agendas, of course) that effectively &quot;translated&quot; what each of them was saying so it made sense to the others.<br /> <br /> It was sometimes hilarious to run, as the translation wasn't perfect. I ran it by having a character talk, then telling each of the others what they heard and understood instead of what was actually said. The SoE was the best, as a lot of what he said I ended up just translating as &quot;incomprehensible technobabble&quot; (described often as, &quot;if this was a comic and dialogue was in word balloons, his would be filled with circuit diagrams and equations instead of words....&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T01:32:10-08:00","id":1017998,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all your answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12015-elstren","name":"Elstren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T03:48:08-08:00","id":1018015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1016050#post1016050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocracy has psionics; they aren't in the spotlight though. The 2nd Progenitor Convention Book has a psionic in the introduction short story - it is mentioned that he needs to synthesize replacement spinal fluid for himself as a result of using his powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that was the form that using Life to heal the damage from Paradox took.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:27:35-08:00","id":1018043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1017633#post1017633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the whole modern psionic telepathy... Well, it's in the books and it's considered a line of research that was previously pursued back in the MK-ULTRA, Cold War era, espionage times, even going so far as beginning to introduce it to the Masses. But it's also stated that it was deep-sixed to a large degree. Taken off the Time Table, etc. It seems like it's a smaller version of what happened to the Etherites, without the consequences... Which means there are definitely some Technocrats out there who were involved in the research (and they might be pissed off that their research was just defunded and de-authorized and all their work left hanging, unless that got conditioned away). The research is also still out there in some NWO Black Archive. There is also a reason why it was taken off the Time Table. if you are a Technephandi fan, maybe the Nephandi masters realized it might increase the chance of their exposure? Otherwise... something happened. Someone make an argument and it was accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Union deep-sixed Psionic research from the Time Table for a much more pragmatic reason: Psychic Powers is one of those things that give the superstitionists a blank check to do all sorts of blatant wizardry.<br /> <br /> If psychic research became more than just fringe science - if governments, universities, and corporations could allocate funding to it openly, and not be laughed at - that affects the Consensus in a big way. Legitimize telekinesis, and every wizard on a broom or a carpet could fly around willy nilly. Same with telepathy, pyrokinesis, technopathy, and remote viewing. Sure, the Technocracy would have this kind of power, but so would their ideological enemies. Let Psionics enter the Consensus, and the Traditions have carte blanche to use their backwards magics as much as they want. If the power is in the mind, then everything a Mystic does is Coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:44:51-08:00","id":1018211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018043#post1018043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Union deep-sixed Psionic research from the Time Table for a much more pragmatic reason: Psychic Powers is one of those things that give the superstitionists a blank check to do all sorts of blatant wizardry.<br /> <br /> If psychic research became more than just fringe science - if governments, universities, and corporations could allocate funding to it openly, and not be laughed at - that affects the Consensus in a big way. Legitimize telekinesis, and every wizard on a broom or a carpet could fly around willy nilly. Same with telepathy, pyrokinesis, technopathy, and remote viewing. Sure, the Technocracy would have this kind of power, but so would their ideological enemies. Let Psionics enter the Consensus, and the Traditions have carte blanche to use their backwards magics as much as they want. If the power is in the mind, then everything a Mystic does is Coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorta the Technocratic Paradigm segues into the Purple Paradigm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T11:25:25-08:00","id":1018523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018043#post1018043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Union deep-sixed Psionic research from the Time Table for a much more pragmatic reason: Psychic Powers is one of those things that give the superstitionists a blank check to do all sorts of blatant wizardry.<br /> <br /> If psychic research became more than just fringe science - if governments, universities, and corporations could allocate funding to it openly, and not be laughed at - that affects the Consensus in a big way. Legitimize telekinesis, and every wizard on a broom or a carpet could fly around willy nilly. Same with telepathy, pyrokinesis, technopathy, and remote viewing. Sure, the Technocracy would have this kind of power, but so would their ideological enemies. Let Psionics enter the Consensus, and the Traditions have carte blanche to use their backwards magics as much as they want. If the power is in the mind, then everything a Mystic does is Coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>A more practical reason would be that it was easier for Mages to infiltrate Technocracy groups - especially those consisting wholly of sympathizers or Extraordinary Citizens - by claiming to be a psion. Especially Cultists of Ecstasy or Sons of the Ether. At the same time, Technocrats having close contact with the Traditions were more prone to defecting when they could not mark a clear line between mystic Magick techniques and Union-approved psionic methods.<br /> <br /> The situation that you described made me think of a post-modern era of witch-hunts that would start with &quot;Prove your psionic powers by levitating without the broom!&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1017633#post1017633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is also a reason why it was taken off the Time Table. if you are a Technephandi fan, maybe the Nephandi masters realized it might increase the chance of their exposure?</div> </div> </div> </div>---&gt; You're implying that proven Technocratic methods of Inspired psychology et al. used by the New World Order can't detect the Nephandi reliably and surely...Care to explain yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-18-2016, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T02:24:20-08:00","id":1018745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018523#post1018523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more practical reason would be that it was easier for Mages to infiltrate Technocracy groups - especially those consisting wholly of sympathizers or Extraordinary Citizens - by claiming to be a psion. Especially Cultists of Ecstasy or Sons of the Ether. At the same time, Technocrats having close contact with the Traditions were more prone to defecting when they could not mark a clear line between mystic Magick techniques and Union-approved psionic methods.?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Technocracy also would have an easier time infiltrating the Traditions with psionic operatives instead of those that are way more dependant on techonlogy.<br /> <br /> Which is, concidentally, still a thing I have a hard time wrapping my head around when it comes to the Grey Suits. I mean...<br /> Here we have the operatives of the most rigid, paranoid, Technocracy-partyline-thumping, technology-is-everything, our-paradigm-is-right, you-must-not-deviate convention.<br /> And now we make part of them people who are supposed to infiltrate and blend into the Traditions.<br /> Alright. This somehow works. Okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T02:49:40-08:00","id":1018746,"title":"","content":"Another telepathy idea: Progenitors can take your DNA sample and vat-grow a copy of your brain. Then they can (with help from other Conventions, perhaps) tune in to the unique frequency you give off and target you with some long-distance particles or waves. They can also run simulations about how you think and decide, and plunder your memory. (if you go with the idea that memory would be stored in DNA). Drug concoctions can be prepared, that are customized to effect you in precise ways.<br /> They can also create a clone of yours to do the above things.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018745#post1018745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, the Technocracy also would have an easier time infiltrating the Traditions with psionic operatives instead of those that are way more dependant on techonlogy.<br /> <br /> Which is, concidentally, still a thing I have a hard time wrapping my head around when it comes to the Grey Suits. I mean...<br /> Here we have the operatives of the most rigid, paranoid, Technocracy-partyline-thumping, technology-is-everything, our-paradigm-is-right, you-must-not-deviate convention.<br /> And now we make part of them people who are supposed to infiltrate and blend into the Traditions.<br /> Alright. This somehow works. Okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is weird about it? I imagine someone having Mind 3+ has no problem hiding her true views. Though I can see how discussing Magickal theory and practices might be problematic - as Grey Suits would have to learn it themselves for best effect. The difficulty of doing so might make Grey Suits rare - or it might not be difficult at all for the NWO, considering they have a variety of Mind Procedures that would aid them with it. The rigidness of the NWO would be good in this case - as it would serve to assure the loyalty of someone who knows much about the Tradition's points of view.<br /> I wonder whether they actually learn Tradition rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-18-2016, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T02:55:21-08:00","id":1018748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018746#post1018746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is weird about it? I imagine someone having Mind 3+ has no problem hiding her true views.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's not the problem, their Mind training and incredible self-control are *perfect* for infiltration. A++.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I can see how discussing Magickal theory and practices might be problematic - as Grey Suits would have to learn it themselves for best effect. I wondered whether they actually learn Tradition rotes. </div> </div> </div>That. Even if they are perfectly fine at hiding their intentions and playing it cool, how do they blend in when it comes to actually discussing the practices and craft they are supposed to play the part of? How are they actually pulling off supposed mystic feats while being dependant on technology? Technology that they also need to hide? Remember, even if they learn about the common rotes of the Tradition they are supposed to hide amongst, it's not like they can actually use those rotes as they are, if they are highly mystic...<br /> <br /> I can see them having an easy time infiltrating the SoE and VA, for obvious reasons - But then we come to groups like Dreamspeakers, Verbena...<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT to add:<br /> And that's a gap Psionic Extraordinary Citizens, and Enlightened Operatives that fall onto that freaky side of things can fill. Definitely a higher risk of defection than a Grey Suit (where it's probably near zero..), but also a much easier way of blending in stylistically and rethorically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-18-2016, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T07:08:58-08:00","id":1018796,"title":"","content":"In the <i>Infinite Tapestry</i> it says how Traditionalists traveling in the Etherspace used to throw suspected infiltrators out of airlocks - because supposedly every mystic is able to breath ether and will survive, while a Technocrat will start suffocating as they are unable to breath because of their Paradigm. It is mentioned that this test is no longer used; and it is the more hidebound Technocrats that find the idea of breathing ether ridiculous. &quot;<i>The boundary between the two philosophies isn't so strictly defined anymore, if it was even true to begin with.</i>&quot; (I wonder how many Traditionalists or Orphans suffocated because they failed the Arete roll needed to breath ether.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018748#post1018748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's a gap Psionic Extraordinary Citizens, and Enlightened Operatives that fall onto that freaky side of things can fill. Definitely a higher risk of defection than a Grey Suit (where it's probably near zero..), but also a much easier way of blending in stylistically and rethorically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes psionics are well suited to infiltrating. Though I don't really see a psionic as more capable of discussing things with Tradition members. Even the supposedly &quot;go with the flow&quot; Ecstatics have incredible depth to their philosophy. Either way a Grey Suit would have to be educated in depth about the particulars.<br /> Also, Grey Suits defection is at least 10 % I'd say. It's hard not to take a liking/respect to Mages while living among them...especially those that work out who you are and start using Mind on you. (including Mind 5 to let you see the other perspective..)<br /> <br /> You can also have Grey Suits pretend to be acolytes, menials or consors. Or pretend to be a former Ghoul, a Nephandic servant 'rescued' by the Mages, or a Kinfolk wanting to ditch the Garou.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018748#post1018748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are they actually pulling off supposed mystic feats while being dependant on technology? Technology that they also need to hide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hide the technology in plain sight if you have to. Keep in Mind that an NWO can constantly use Mind Adjustments to make sure no questions are asked - they might have impressive and touching stories on each of their 'foci', to the point when they might be complemented and respected because of their style of Magick!<br /> -All of the first levels of the Spheres can be simulated with biologically modified or cybernetic eyes. (or other body modifications \u2013 it could be any of the senses) Entropy might be more complex, but there is an Adjustment in the new Syndicate books that allows a Syndic to compute probabilities during a firefight; so you can implant such a device into a Grey Suit's brain or inside a mystical-looking item.<br /> <br /> -Carrying a supposed mystic foci for Prime while having a Primal Energy device implanted inside you. Each time you hold the crystal to call upon Prime, you also engage the device. The device is recharged by the Tradition node or Tass normally.<br /> <br /> -Spirit seems impossible - Void Engineer devices seem quite bulky, and spirits could sense the deception. Though if you want, Spirit 1 can be technological glasses pretending to be mystical, and for other effects mystic-looking crystals - or ominous carved black boxes \u2013 filled with Dimensional Science tech can be used.<br /> <br /> -Time - say that you can only divine events in regards to people you have a connection to. Predict what people will do using Inspired psychology, while for appearance sake doing some ridiculously over-complicated Tarot spread, that you also prearrange cards for so that what you get matches your predictions. If you're afraid of a Tarot authority busting you, you can instead take something like Magic the Gathering cards.<br /> You can also have a hidden chronometric device which you use while alone, and then you say you discovered something during a trance. It could be overt \u2013 like a seemingly mystical crystal globe that has technology for Time 2 that shows events at a location. Time 3 bullet time or extra actions can be simulated easily with implanted tech or drugs made to look mystical. Rewinding or freezing time devices, if they exist, are too bulky for infiltrations I imagine.<br /> <br /> -Mind - same as Time for mind reading. For Mind influencing you might have to use other methods, like psionics or pheromones \u2013 it's hard to simulate Vulgar or near-Vulgar Mind with NWO Adjustments, especially since you won't be able to pretend to call upon the usual governmental authority. Or you can say that it disagrees with you to influence someone's mind, and thus you can only read minds.<br /> <br /> -Technocratic compounds/nanomachines disguised as alchemy for Matter. A technologically bulletproof hoodie can be adorned with 'mystic runes' etc. Such hoodies can even be given out to Mages or Acolytes for protection.<br /> <br /> -Life: use Technocratic mixtures or nanomachine batches put into colorful potions.Cybernetics or other Progenitor alterations can be made to look mystic. All it takes is having an retractable extra arm that seems to come from a mystic ritual (that you faithfully 'cast' every week to maintain it) to convince Traditionalists you have mystic Life 3.<br /> <br /> -Forces \u2013 the wand or dagger you carry might have a particle (de)accelarator implanted inside. Those functions can be engaged with a mind impulse, while pretending to use it mystically. Explosions can be created by putting a super-volatile compound into the air.<br /> <br /> -A Correspondence: Data device modified to look like a mirror. You can even keep the interface, just make it look all mystic.<br /> <br /> -Entropy 1 divinations can be faked as mystic just like Time. Entropy 2 and 3 probability manipulations I don't really see as fakeable, as Technocrats need lots of preparation time and resources to do them, as far as I know. Entropy 3 disrupting machines can be faked with an electromagnetic pulse \u2013 just hope that nobody has Forces sight active while you are doing it.<br /> <br /> As an interesting option, you can have the supposedly fake mystic foci actually work, possibly cause they put so much technical effort into them - like the Tarot spread showing Prince of Cups, the Moon and the Tower, despite being prearranged differently. This would indicate a Malkavian Prince planning to make the Chantry target of the Camarilla. What will the Technocrat do? Especially since the Mages will give him great respect as they also divine in this direction, confirm the danger, and ward against it.<br /> Or the 'fake' Prime crystal working for Prime even after the implanted Primal Energy device malfunctions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Traditions scanning foci for technology might be a problem. Is it said anywhere that Technocrats can't learn mystic Spheres at all? In the end this is also a possibility \u2013 the Order of Reason knowingly used scrying/projection crystals for Correspondence because it was just too good of a capability to deny themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-18-2016, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T07:29:27-08:00","id":1018803,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's difficult for any infiltrator to replicate the mystic arts without practicing them for real. Trying to use a tech Instrument on a sly is problematic, because anyone with Life or Matter senses would be able to notice 95-99% of what a Technocrat would use. If you've got a gizmo in your pocket or an implant in your brain, that kind of thing can be seen by many beginners. Same with genetic rewrites or bio-mods. Like Ambrosia said, trying to pass yourself off as a Virtual Adept or Etherite is doable - most of your equipment would just need minor cosmetic work to make it look shittier - but mystics are right out.<br /> <br /> An NWO can't wave a bone around or chant in Latin and be able to accomplish anything. Not unless they know and believe in the mystic Focus. And when infiltrators start learning their enemy's world view to the point where they believe in it themselves, Going Native is not just a possibility, but a virtual certainty. Not unless they've undergone high level Mind Procedures to compartmentalize their consciousness, creating clear personality boundaries between the part that believes in the mystical mumbo jumbo, and the part that believes in science.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018796#post1018796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hide the technology in plain sight if you have to. Keep in Mind that an NWO can constantly use Mind Adjustments to make sure no questions are asked - they might have impressive and touching stories on each of their 'foci', to the point when they might be complemented and respected because of their style of Magick!<br /> -All of the first levels of the Spheres can be simulated with biologically modified or cybernetic eyes. (or other body modifications \u2013 it could be any of the senses) Entropy might be more complex, but there is an Adjustment in the new Syndicate books that allows a Syndic to compute probabilities during a firefight; so you can implant such a device into a Grey Suit's brain or inside a mystical-looking item.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said above, a vast majority of the possibilities you listed can be spotted with Life 1 or Matter 1. If your &quot;magic wand&quot; is hollow, hiding a sonic screwdriver inside, Matter 1's basic function allows the user to see what an object is made of. Including hidden compartments or features. At any time, a Tradition mage could happen to have that sense active - there are plenty of reasons why they would, incidental to the infiltrator's presence - and happen to look over at the spy.<br /> <br /> At that point, the best the Technocrat could hope for is that the Traditionalist fails their Perception + Alertness roll to notice the fact that the wand is a fake. Every single time.<br /> <br /> Same with a mechanical (or biological) implant, or nanomachines in the bloodstream. That sort of radical reorganization of one's body would get noticed by anyone who had the relevant sense spells active. And the moment the character's augmentation or fake mystic tools are discovered, it raises questions. Uncomfortable questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-18-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:04:58-08:00","id":1018810,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, a Technocrat infiltrator would have a much easier time avoiding the above pitfalls by simply pretending to be a member of one of the many technomancer factions within otherwise mystic Traditions. House Thig/Verditus, the Lhaksmists, Techno-shamans, the Alexandrian Society, etc. Groups that otherwise adhere to the basic worldview of their parent groups, but who blend them with modern technology. In this case, it would pay to make the integration of technology and traditional tools <i>more obvious</i>. Hiding in plain sight, as it were.<br /> <br /> One problem: the Traditionalists rarely fully trust their technomancer kin. At best. Likely for the very same reason they seem so tempting to infiltrate as. I'm willing to bet the Traditions have been burned by this sort of thing before, and are on their guard. Even if they don't know for certain that the technomancer in question is a spy, many would rather avoid giving them too much information. Part of this is just blind prejudice, certainly, but even that works unknowingly in the Traditions' favor when it comes to actual infiltrators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:35:29-08:00","id":1018820,"title":"","content":"If Technocrats can block and fool telepathy, shouldn't they also be able to create materials and items that fool Matter, Life and Correspondence senses? I'll admit that it's easier to imagine blocking mind reading because of how the mind is not a physical thing...but at the same time for mystic Mind users it is a concrete thing, that they can see...yet Grey Suits are (I assume, otherwise there would be no way to infiltrate reliably) able to block mystical mind reading through technological or mental means.<br /> The items might have a design that utilizes Correspondence to refer viewers to a sub-space with a normally looking item. A material might block mystical senses from perceiving it (maybe Primium could be used). A tiny device inside could generate some sort of field that blocks mystical perception for the whole item. Then the Technocrat can say that it must be a property of his foci that you can't really see them fully with mystical senses. The nanomachines in the bloodstream might be made to look and behave just like normal cells or bacteria in the body; or they can be modified to work on such a tiny sub-dimensional level that Life and Matter can only detect them if they are used for Vulgar effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-18-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:42:02-08:00","id":1018844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018803#post1018803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's difficult for any infiltrator to replicate the mystic arts without practicing them for real. Trying to use a tech Instrument on a sly is problematic, because anyone with Life or Matter senses would be able to notice 95-99% of what a Technocrat would use. If you've got a gizmo in your pocket or an implant in your brain, that kind of thing can be seen by many beginners. Same with genetic rewrites or bio-mods. Like Ambrosia said, trying to pass yourself off as a Virtual Adept or Etherite is doable - most of your equipment would just need minor cosmetic work to make it look shittier - but mystics are right out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Mind 3 so they ignore the technological Instrument (or whatever) and pay attention to the false front actions that mimic whatever superstitious nonsense they believe makes the effect work. <br /> <br /> Use Instruments that they segue with their beliefs. It's not hard to infiltrate the Ecstatics if you're also using drugs, acoustics and hypnogogic states, . <br /> <br /> Have your Instruments in place and have the action the Tradition mages expect just serve as the activation threshold. Yup, I cut my hand and X happens, but it wasn't superstitious mumbo-jumbo that caused it happen, it was the neurochemical trigger on the nanotech mods to my otherwise perfectly normal red blood cells. <br /> <br /> Just use relatively innocuous Instruments and appropriate window dressing to make it seem like adherence to paradigm. Those blessed bullets with the crosses carved into them that cement my Warrior of the Lord cover ID? Those are actually precision crafted in my personally configured firearm in tandem with my specialized mental state training.<br /> <br /> Infiltrating the Dreamspeakers is going to be difficult to impossible without something extreme, but cross-Traditions cabals aren't uncommon. So don't try. Have an ID that can make friends with a Dreamspeaker and infiltrate that way. Very, very carefully.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with any sort of infiltration is the game's party line that the Technocracy doesn't believe in the reality of magic, even though they clearly can observe it's existence, particularly under these circumstances. (But then that is a big problem with the Union as presented at all. As, technically speaking, they should be willfully blind to anything &quot;magical&quot; or justification machines with a psychopathic level of belief in extreme proximate cause and conspiracy theory.... and they don't have any Prime or Awareness, etc.) The MiGs have to be in on the Big Lie or they can't really function in this manner at all. Or you have to change this trope and, say, just have the Union party line be more along the lines of &quot;We do the same thing. We do it with reasonable protocols and concern for safety. They, however, do it in archaic and inherently dangerous ways.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T21:56:00-08:00","id":1019054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1018844#post1018844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use Mind 3 so they ignore the technological Instrument (or whatever) and pay attention to the false front actions that mimic whatever superstitious nonsense they believe makes the effect work.<br /> <br /> Use Instruments that they segue with their beliefs. It's not hard to infiltrate the Ecstatics if you're also using drugs, acoustics and hypnogogic states, .<br /> <br /> Have your Instruments in place and have the action the Tradition mages expect just serve as the activation threshold. Yup, I cut my hand and X happens, but it wasn't superstitious mumbo-jumbo that caused it happen, it was the neurochemical trigger on the nanotech mods to my otherwise perfectly normal red blood cells.<br /> <br /> Just use relatively innocuous Instruments and appropriate window dressing to make it seem like adherence to paradigm. Those blessed bullets with the crosses carved into them that cement my Warrior of the Lord cover ID? Those are actually precision crafted in my personally configured firearm in tandem with my specialized mental state training.<br /> <br /> Infiltrating the Dreamspeakers is going to be difficult to impossible without something extreme, but cross-Traditions cabals aren't uncommon. So don't try. Have an ID that can make friends with a Dreamspeaker and infiltrate that way. Very, very carefully.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with any sort of infiltration is the game's party line that the Technocracy doesn't believe in the reality of magic, even though they clearly can observe it's existence, particularly under these circumstances. (But then that is a big problem with the Union as presented at all. As, technically speaking, they should be willfully blind to anything &quot;magical&quot; or justification machines with a psychopathic level of belief in extreme proximate cause and conspiracy theory.... and they don't have any Prime or Awareness, etc.) The MiGs have to be in on the Big Lie or they can't really function in this manner at all. Or you have to change this trope and, say, just have the Union party line be more along the lines of &quot;We do the same thing. We do it with reasonable protocols and concern for safety. They, however, do it in archaic and inherently dangerous ways.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, except I question the credibility of any plan that relies on using Mind to fool Mages, when anyone with Mind 1 could have the chance of realizing their perceptions and thoughts are being tampered with. The tactic would work on some Traditionalists, yes, and a sufficiently skilled MiG could make their Effect subtle enough to get past many mental defenses unnoticed. But with this approach, the infiltrator has a delicate tightrope walking ahead of them. If you have to fool a whole cabal of Mages, the Effect is rolled against the highest Willpower in the room (which, as we all know, is always a base 5, likely higher with any Mage of appreciable experience). Failure (during any given instance of attempting this charade) means one or more of the &quot;audience&quot; realizes the infiltrator is screwing with their perceptions, even if they don't know how. And people tend to take that sort of thing badly, even if they don't yet suspect infiltration. Hitting someone with a Mind trick - for any reason - implies a duplicity that a spy cannot afford.<br /> <br /> What I've been trying to get across is that an infiltrator has their work cut out for them if they try to <i>fake</i> a mystical Focus entirely. Spies in the Real World(TM) try to have their cover identities and stories be as close to the truth as possible for the same reason. Any irregularity arouses suspicion, as it calls the spy's word into question. This is why Technocrats masquerading as technomystics is the safest means of infiltration. They don't need to layer Procedures onto their tools, nor do they need to answer uncomfortable questions if they ever fail (or are simply noticed, as noticing a lie can be almost as damaging to one's cover as the actual truth being known). This is why Technocrats prefer to go undercover as Etherite or Virtual Adept members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T04:15:35-08:00","id":1019152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1019054#post1019054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, except I question the credibility of any plan that relies on using Mind to fool Mages, when anyone with Mind 1 could have the chance of realizing their perceptions and thoughts are being tampered with. The tactic would work on some Traditionalists, yes, and a sufficiently skilled MiG could make their Effect subtle enough to get past many mental defenses unnoticed. But with this approach, the infiltrator has a delicate tightrope walking ahead of them. If you have to fool a whole cabal of Mages, the Effect is rolled against the highest Willpower in the room (which, as we all know, is always a base 5, likely higher with any Mage of appreciable experience). Failure (during any given instance of attempting this charade) means one or more of the &quot;audience&quot; realizes the infiltrator is screwing with their perceptions, even if they don't know how. And people tend to take that sort of thing badly, even if they don't yet suspect infiltration. Hitting someone with a Mind trick - for any reason - implies a duplicity that a spy cannot afford.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this.<br /> While a Grey Suit can hide their own thoughts preeeeetty darn well, you run into serious issues if the same infiltrator starts using 'nothing to see here' mind effects on *others*. Mental Shields. Installed Wonders in Chantries that sound the klaxons if newcomers use Mind Magick on somebody else.<br /> The issue is that mages are *the* WOD splat with the biggest figurative sensor array of magick detectors, life sensors and what have you. it makes infiltration a very, very, very hard thing to pull off. Especially with offensive Mind effects. That'd be *the* thing I'd gear a Chantry's internal defenses for. Combine with a thourough screening of newcomers for hidden technological devices and a thorough Mind-scan (Which, as I said, might be the one thing a Grey Suit is very skilled at falsifying..), and..it's just a toughie.<br /> <br /> Of course, as an ST, you can simply hand-wave some things...but the thing is that both sides of the coin are supposed to be playable as protagonists, so the ST can't quite handwave...you will run into exactly those issues as a Technocracy character player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:16:16-08:00","id":1019280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1019054#post1019054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, except I question the credibility of any plan that relies on using Mind to fool Mages, when anyone with Mind 1 could have the chance of realizing their perceptions and thoughts are being tampered with. The tactic would work on some Traditionalists, yes, and a sufficiently skilled MiG could make their Effect subtle enough to get past many mental defenses unnoticed. But with this approach, the infiltrator has a delicate tightrope walking ahead of them. If you have to fool a whole cabal of Mages, the Effect is rolled against the highest Willpower in the room (which, as we all know, is always a base 5, likely higher with any Mage of appreciable experience). Failure (during any given instance of attempting this charade) means one or more of the &quot;audience&quot; realizes the infiltrator is screwing with their perceptions, even if they don't know how. And people tend to take that sort of thing badly, even if they don't yet suspect infiltration. Hitting someone with a Mind trick - for any reason - implies a duplicity that a spy cannot afford.<br /> <br /> What I've been trying to get across is that an infiltrator has their work cut out for them if they try to <i>fake</i> a mystical Focus entirely. Spies in the Real World(TM) try to have their cover identities and stories be as close to the truth as possible for the same reason. Any irregularity arouses suspicion, as it calls the spy's word into question. This is why Technocrats masquerading as technomystics is the safest means of infiltration. They don't need to layer Procedures onto their tools, nor do they need to answer uncomfortable questions if they ever fail (or are simply noticed, as noticing a lie can be almost as damaging to one's cover as the actual truth being known). This is why Technocrats prefer to go undercover as Etherite or Virtual Adept members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick a group of younger mages without those capabilities. Effortless to find out. Just have your MiBs working with recon it out at every level before infiltration (surveillance, sousveillance, a few well-placed attacks to test out their capabilities). Focus is highly individualized. Just make it long term. If your buddies trust you, they'll trust the peculiar way you do things. They will be doing their own peculiar things. And they'll defend your weirdness to other mages, if you are playing your cards right. After all, you don't have to rely on Hypertech or Cybernetics as the Practices... Art of Desire/Hypereconomics, Dominion and Reality Hacking and possibly Martial Arts or even Yoga all will fly under the radar much more easily. Instruments help out too... Drugs and poisons, books and periodicals, dances and movement, eye contact, formulae and math, Household (or mundane) tools, language, meditation, social domination, voice and vocalizations and so on. And that's where the &quot;fool them twice&quot; works really well. Do what they expect and they'll think it's working how they expect it to, even if, as far as you're concerned, it's working for a completely different reason. Make THEM have to invade YOUR mind to find out that you don't have the proper 'think&quot; going. After all, that's rather rude, at best...<br /> <br /> The best asset? The Nine Traditions have no internal organization in a meaningful &quot;on the ground&quot; way. None. At all. Compare it to the average other splat... Vampires and their cities, Wraiths and their necropoli, Werewolves and their Caerns, Changelings and their Freeholds. Chantries across towns don't have to have any relation to each other at all. Or even be aware of each other. Much less any other cabals that might be in the area. And since Mage is explicitly not supposed to be a location-based game (according to Brucato) that means that almost every cabal is just passing through from here to there and their path across the Tapestry, that makes the Nine Traditions at the fine grain EXTREMELY easy to infiltrate. It's barely a confederacy at the highest end. Sure, SOME of the individual Traditions arguably have internal organization, but that doesn't cross Tradition lines for the most part. And a large number of the Traditions are a complete organizational mess. The most well-organized loci are the Chantries, particularly large, powerful, old and well-organized Chantries are going to be a problem. So avoid them. That's why you start with a small independent group and move them towards that as an end goal. If you only need to get into Horizon for a single info grab, that's doable. Dangerous, but doable. If you want to take the Seat of Matter... good luck. <br /> <br /> It also might be better to stay away from VA's and Sons of Ether. Sure, they do machines too, but the Union ways of doing machine are consistent. Theirs are idiosyncratic. The fact that you're not doing weird individualistic stuff will make you stand out. Both have really bad histories with the Union and apt to be more on the look out, as much as they can be, for infiltration. And the hoary old types in the Chantries of the other Traditions think VA's and SoE's are barely &quot;real&quot; mages either, johnny-come-lately refugees from the Union and are therefore easier for the Union to infiltrate. So they are looking out for you more internally and externally in those two groups. Sure, the jacket may be closer to the skill set required, but... Easier to fit in. Easier to get caught.<br /> <br /> How about trying something like.... An Arete 4 MiG finds a small cabal of low level Disciples (Arete 2-3)with minimal current contact with well-organized older Chantries, locates a small vulnerable Chantry or cabal and has it destroyed, arranges for the cabal to get there &quot;too late&quot; and all they can do is help the &quot;only survivor&quot;, a Hermetic from House Tytalus who uses a lot of social domination, eye contact, reads his American Psychology Association monthly along with his studies of the kabbala (no reason not to see if there isn't something &quot;salvageable&quot; for &quot;real magic&quot; from the modern drek, right?.... Along with a &quot;know thy enemy&quot;....), voice and vocalizations (sure THEY think he's saying Words of Power, but he KNOWS it's just kinesics and using sonic cues to active certain patterns of behavior that are either hardwired into the human brain or have been literally programmed in when the subject was eating his Wheaties as a child...), etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:21:19-08:00","id":1019342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/10192-ask-me-a-trivia-question#post10192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Art of Desire/Hypereconomics, Dominion and Reality Hacking and possibly Martial Arts or even Yoga all will fly under the radar much more easily. Instruments help out too... Drugs and poisons, books and periodicals, dances and movement, eye contact, formulae and math, Household (or mundane) tools, language, meditation, social domination, voice and vocalizations and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>NWO could create a facade Hermetic House, or a fake Craft, based on those practices...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T12:42:53-08:00","id":1019369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1019342#post1019342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NWO could create a facade Hermetic House, or a fake Craft, based on those practices...</div> </div> </div> </div>In Re: A new House? Why bother? That's a lot of work. I'm sure that raising a group from Ex Misc or adopting a group en masse from outside gets some level of vetting. Particularly if they don't have a hoary pedigree of ancient antecedents. That's a really long term mass infiltration, organized by Control, not a MiG mission. More like (a TON o' MiG missions, a team of MiW on oversight, etc.) <br /> <br /> As for making a Craft... Sure, why not? It won't accomplish the same goals. Not really good for infiltrating the Nine Traditions. Probably make it pretty easy to smash the Disparate Alliance into splinters pretty effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T14:36:09-08:00","id":1022461,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Disparate Craft based on the MK-ULTRA conspiracies that uses psionics as the lynchpin for their Magick. They combine mysticism with pseudo-scientific explanations as to how it works. According to all of them, it's ALL psionic activity. The hows of this vary from member to member.<br /> <br /> The fun part is: they were initially started by a joint effort of the Progenitors/NWO, but enough of the Awakened members hid and organized a group of their own. So they aren't much for the Traditions, but they FEAR the Technocracy. (They have some &quot;dubious allies&quot; in the Society of Ether and Cult of Ecstasy.) The Disparates are about their speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 12-26-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:19:05-08:00","id":1022794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016043-telepathy-and-the-technocracy?p=1022461#post1022461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for a Disparate Craft based on the MK-ULTRA conspiracies that uses psionics as the lynchpin for their Magick. They combine mysticism with pseudo-scientific explanations as to how it works. According to all of them, it's ALL psionic activity. The hows of this vary from member to member.<br /> <br /> The fun part is: they were initially started by a joint effort of the Progenitors/NWO, but enough of the Awakened members hid and organized a group of their own. So they aren't much for the Traditions, but they FEAR the Technocracy. (They have some &quot;dubious allies&quot; in the Society of Ether and Cult of Ecstasy.) The Disparates are about their speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>These guys would be so ripe for Nephandic corruption. A la MAJESTIC in Delta Green.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:26:37-08:00","id":1024499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbco